in the next few hours, she would transcend to even a higher level of drumming....I will always remember her when I drum...may Allah fill her heart  with the awesome drumming of the Divine Heart Beat....]]></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>&#8230;from the deepest heart of my heart&#8230;.we shared so many times , when she guided &amp; saw after our &#8216; Sufi healing list&#8217;&#8230;my first &#8216;Leaders / Shafayat retreat&#8217; in Seattle 2010, we met. She sang as I played drums&#8230;.one day she called me to say thanks for the drumming during that gathering, I was totally amazed, that the sounds that came from that small drum touched her so much&#8230;I said if U like that drumming, then check a short clip on &#8216;you tube&#8217;&#8230;much too my surprise &amp; awakening, she did almost immediately&#8230;she called back with a few minutes &amp; said&#8221; oh, that&#8217;s good&#8217;, but your drumming from our time together still rings in my head &amp; I can&#8217;t seem to want to hear anything else&#8230;<br />
in the next few hours, she would transcend to even a higher level of drumming&#8230;.I will always remember her when I drum&#8230;may Allah fill her heart  with the awesome drumming of the Divine Heart Beat&#8230;.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
