		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://remembrance.sufipaths.net/?page_id=829#comment-8547</guid>
		<description><![CDATA[Our beloved Sufi sister Carol McGonegal passed away peacefully yesterday morning, at home, with her beloved husband Colby by her side. I, we, will miss her loving presence greatly. Carol was a Shefayat in the Sufi Healing Order. She kept the Sufi Order International Healing list going for many, many years. People from all over the world brought names to the list she cared for so thoroughly and well. 

Carol was a master practitioner and teacher of Tai Chi, a pillar of her family and community, and a kind, compassionate friend. As she approached her passing she was full of light and wisdom. The perfume of her being lingers in this world 

Amida Cary]]></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>Our beloved Sufi sister Carol McGonegal passed away peacefully yesterday morning, at home, with her beloved husband Colby by her side. I, we, will miss her loving presence greatly. Carol was a Shefayat in the Sufi Healing Order. She kept the Sufi Order International Healing list going for many, many years. People from all over the world brought names to the list she cared for so thoroughly and well. </p>
<p>Carol was a master practitioner and teacher of Tai Chi, a pillar of her family and community, and a kind, compassionate friend. As she approached her passing she was full of light and wisdom. The perfume of her being lingers in this world </p>
<p>Amida Cary</p>
]]></content:encoded>
